node_modules
node_modules/

# ── Derived, and fully regenerable ──────────────────────────────────────────
#   npm run assets   rebuilds public/img from the product photography in the
#                    repository root, measuring every size off the file
#   npm run audio    rebuilds the bed, the cue layer and the silent VO slot
# Together these are ~90 MB of output carrying no information the recipes lack.
public/img/
public/audio/music-bed-*.mp3
public/audio/transitions-*.wav
public/vo/*.wav

# public/audio/sfx/ is NOT derived — it is the cue palette cut for the Soundcraft
# Signature Plus films, and it is an input to this one. public/fonts/ is an input
# too: a render must never depend on fetching a typeface over the network.
# public/broll/ is where the ten deployment clips land. Both are committed.

# ── Render intermediates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
out/*-chunks/
out/*-silent.mp4

# ── The masters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB, and the brief asked for the uncompressed
# original rather than a smaller version of it — so a master that does not fit
# is CUT, never squeezed.
#
# Cut by BYTES, not into playable segments. ffmpeg -f segment is the obvious
# answer and it is wrong: each segment carries its own AAC encoder priming, so
# rejoining them does not give back the master. Measured on the 89.9 s reel,
# the rejoin came out 1024 samples — one AAC frame, 21.3 ms — LONGER, and 99.5%
# of its samples differed from the original, worst case -0.9 dBFS. The picture
# rejoined bit-identically; the sound drifted 21 ms against it for the whole
# back half of the film.
#
# A byte split has no opinion about codecs, priming or timestamps, so the
# concatenation IS the original file and sha256 proves it:
#
#     cd out/motu-ultralite828-explainer-parts && ./rejoin.sh
#
# The price is that a part does not play on its own, which is why a single-file
# 1080p viewing copy ships beside each master — nobody should have to rejoin
# anything just to watch the film.
#
#     npm run verify:parts motu-ultralite828-explainer   proves the rejoin
#
out/motu-ultralite828-explainer.mp4
